 "notes": "floor_stability recast the standing-spread question as a rate problem. This maps the rate surface: floor height x flow x seed, crown surface only, on the recovered cell (d280 + vacancy reposts). A floor that opens the band on every draw of both flows is structural; a floor that only works under split flow is fragile. Measured: the rate is MONOTONE in floor height \u2014 g12 lands in band on every split draw and 2/3 of iid draws (the first iid cell inside the tape's band); g8 is marginal under iid. The mechanism generalizes \u2014 the earlier g8 cells were simply under-dosed; floor_structural stays FALSE only because no single g hits 1.0 on both flows.",
 "receipt_sha256": "f798b195cbb7aff646f21a2ca848fc8b0faa1f8c9cd505034f5471794af4fd85"
}
